This is a greenfield project — no code exists yet. The chat feature needs supporting infrastructure (DB, auth, etc.) to function. Here's my design:

## Design: Team & Judge Private Chat Channels

**Architecture:** Node.js/Express backend + React/Vite frontend, all under `src/`.

### Backend (`src/backend/`)

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `db.ts` | SQLite via `better-sqlite3`, WAL mode, ChatMessage + Team + Judge tables |
| `middleware/auth.ts` | JWT verification, `requireRole()` helper |
| `middleware/chat.ts` | Channel access validation — `team:{id}` checks JWT `team_id`, `judge` checks role |
| `routes/chat.ts` | `GET/POST /api/chat/team/:teamId/messages`, `GET/POST /api/chat/judge/messages`, `DELETE` for admin |
| `socket.ts` | Socket.io with same auth + channel middleware, real-time broadcast |

### Frontend (`src/frontend/`)

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `pages/TeamChat.tsx` | Message list + input, scoped to `team:{id}`, shows team name in header |
| `pages/JudgeChat.tsx` | Message list + input, scoped to `judge` channel, "JUDGES SECURE COMMS" header |
| `pages/admin/ChatModeration.tsx` | Tabs: Global / per-team / Judge, view all messages, delete any |

### Access Control Logic

- `team:{id}` channel: JWT must have `team_id === parseInt(id)`, or `role === "admin"`
- `judge` channel: JWT `role === "judge"` or `role === "admin"`
- DELETE operations: `role === "admin"` only

### DB Schema (minimal)

```sql
CREATE TABLE teams (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL);
CREATE TABLE judges (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, anonymous_id TEXT UNIQUE);
CREATE TABLE chat_messages (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
  channel TEXT NOT NULL,
  sender_id INTEGER,
  sender_name TEXT NOT NULL,
  sender_role TEXT NOT NULL,
  content TEXT NOT NULL,
  created_at TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now'))
);
```

**Ponytail decisions:**
- No file upload (image/audio) in this milestone — text-only chat. The PRD mentions MinIO but that's a separate milestone concern.
- No Socket.io initially — REST polling (30s interval) for MVP, Socket.io can layer on top later.
- Single `src/` directory structure as requested, not the `frontend/`+`backend/` split from PRD.

Does this approach work? Any adjustments before I implement?
